# Live per-user state never belongs in the shared repo; copy STATE.template.md
# into your projects instead.
STATE.md
# The project store: live per-project state, and never committable. It was
# ignored only through .git/info/exclude on the author's machine until
# 2026-08-08, when the release court's fresh clone proved a stranger hits
# the store's own safety refusal ("git does NOT ignore .brothermode")
# the first time they run BrotherMode inside a clone.
.brothermode/
# Same reason: the work registry records real working paths, which can be
# home directories or client and project names on someone's machine.
threads/
.DS_Store
*.bak*
__pycache__/
.superpowers/
# Build artifacts from `uv build` or `python3 -m build`. They must never be
# committed and they must never be left lying around either: scripts/
# verify-install.sh walks the tree and fails on any entry the manifest does
# not name, so a forgotten build/ directory makes a clean checkout look
# tampered with. See docs/PACKAGING.md.
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
# Generated per-project documentation. Same reason as STATE.md and
# threads/ above: the pages render live store rows, real claimed paths,
# owner names and note authors, which are one machine's working state and
# not shared repository content. Regenerate it with
# `python3 tools/bm_docs.py generate` in any project, including this one.
Documentation/
# V2 (release-closure loop2 refuter fixes): tools/bm_project.py's generated
# views, same reason as STATE.md and Documentation/ above (real project
# rows, not shared repository content). Root-anchored (a leading "/") so
# only THIS repo's own top-level copies are ignored; project-template/'s
# CANVAS.md and DELIVERY-PACKET.md are the shipped template a fresh project
# starts from and stay tracked. The plain and the multi-project
# (CANVAS-<project_id>.md, see C5) filenames are both covered.
/CANVAS.md
/DELIVERY-PACKET.md
/CANVAS-*.md
/DELIVERY-PACKET-*.md
# L05 visual surface: PROJECT-VIEW.html (bm-view render) and the Handover/
# brief pages (bm-view brief-page) are generated views of one machine's live
# project rows, same reason as the CANVAS and Documentation entries above.
/PROJECT-VIEW.html
/Handover/
/Handover-*/
# An export is every row the store holds for one project, and with --raw it
# is the unredacted prose. It is written for its owner, never for a shared
# repository, so the generated name is ignored the same way.
/EXPORT-*.json

# Agent worktrees (2026-08-16). Claude Code creates .claude/worktrees/<agent>
# for isolation-mode subagents, and on this machine they reached 678 MB. The
# rule lived only in .git/info/exclude, which is local and untracked, so every
# other clone and every CI checkout saw them as repository content. A
# BrotherSBE architecture review found this coupling the same day it caused
# three starved gate runs; tools/test_install.py's copytree now skips .claude
# as well, and this line makes the ignore travel with the repository.
.claude/worktrees/
